{"story_id":"KR-51002-050","title":"Three Things Mastered","title_raw":"L       THREE THINGS MASTERED","notes":"","language":"en","original_language":"ko","country":"Korea","country_code":"KR","culture_region":"朝鮮半島","latitude":36.6,"longitude":127.9,"location_precision":"culture_region","map_location_type":"source_culture_region","collector":"Im Bang; Yi Ryuk","translator":"James S. Gale","publication_year":1913,"year_evidence":"扉に 1913(序文の署名は 1911)","book_id":"PG-51002","book_title":"Korean Folk Tales: Imps, Ghosts and Fairies","source_provider":"Project Gutenberg","source_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/51002","source_title":"Korean folk tales : $b Imps, ghosts and fairies","license_status":"PUBLIC_DOMAIN_US","license_name":"Public Domain (United States)","license_jurisdiction":"US","rights_evidence_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/51002","redistribution_allowed":true,"commercial_use":true,"derivative_use":true,"ml_processing_status":"reviewed","verification_date":"2026-09-08","word_count":257,"text":"There was a relative of the king, named Im Sung-jong, who was a gifted\nman in thought and purpose. He was the first performer of his time on\nthe harp. King Se-jong said of him, \"Im's harp knows but one master,\nand follows no other man.\"\n\nHis home was outside the South Gate, and every morning he was seen\nkneeling on the sill of his front door beating his hands upwards and\ndownwards on his knees, and this practice he carried on for three\nyears. People could not imagine what he meant by it, but thought him\nmad. Thus he learned the motions required for the harp.\n\nAlso he blew with his mouth and practised with his fingers day and\nnight without stopping, so that when people called on him he would\nsee them but would not perceive them. He kept this up for three years\nand so learned the motions for the flute.\n\nHe was a lightly built man in body, and poor at riding and at\narchery. He often sighed over this defect, and said, \"Though I am\nweak and stupid and not able to shoot a long distance, I shall yet\nknow how to hit the target and make the bull's-eye. This also must be\nacquired by practice.\" So every morning he took his bow and arrows\nand went off into the hills. There he shot all day long, keeping it\nup for three years, till he became a renowned archer. Thus you may\nperceive the kind of man he was.\n\nYi Ryuk.\n\nLI","cluster":1,"analysis":{"analysis_version":"1.0","embedding_model":"intfloat/multilingual-e5-small","themes":[],"motifs":[],"animals":[],"nature":[{"label":"海","count":1,"method":"count","confidence":1.0}],"events":[{"position":0.0,"label":"Gift","hits":1,"lift":55.59,"method":"count"},{"position":0.091,"label":null,"hits":0,"lift":0.0,"method":"count"},{"position":0.182,"label":null,"hits":0,"lift":0.0,"method":"count"},{"position":0.273,"label":null,"hits":0,"lift":0.0,"method":"count"},{"position":0.364,"label":null,"hits":0,"lift":0.0,"method":"count"},{"position":0.455,"label":null,"hits":0,"lift":0.0,"method":"count"},{"position":0.545,"label":null,"hits":0,"lift":0.0,"method":"count"},{"position":0.636,"label":null,"hits":0,"lift":0.0,"method":"count"},{"position":0.727,"label":null,"hits":0,"lift":0.0,"method":"count"},{"position":0.818,"label":"Trial","hits":1,"lift":32.01,"method":"count"},{"position":0.909,"label":null,"hits":0,"lift":0.0,"method":"count"},{"position":1.0,"label":"Transformation","hits":1,"lift":185.06,"method":"count"}],"tension":[{"position":0.0,"tension":1.0,"raw":0.0,"method":"lexicon"},{"position":0.091,"tension":1.0,"raw":0.0,"method":"lexicon"},{"position":0.182,"tension":1.0,"raw":0.0,"method":"lexicon"},{"position":0.273,"tension":1.0,"raw":0.0,"method":"lexicon"},{"position":0.364,"tension":1.0,"raw":0.0,"method":"lexicon"},{"position":0.455,"tension":1.0,"raw":0.0,"method":"lexicon"},{"position":0.545,"tension":1.0,"raw":0.0,"method":"lexicon"},{"position":0.636,"tension":1.0,"raw":0.0,"method":"lexicon"},{"position":0.727,"tension":1.0,"raw":